            "question_id": "sq:measurement:method-inappropriate",
            "question": "Was the method of measuring the outcome inappropriate?",
            "driver": false,
            "answer": "probably_no",
            "facts": [],
            "warrant": "The composite includes objectively recorded death and a protocol-defined BPD component at 36 weeks PMA. BPD criteria incorporate oxygen/respiratory-support thresholds after at least 28 days of support; where oxygen need is subjective, an oxygen-reduction test confirms dependency using an oxygen-saturation threshold. This is a structured, clinically relevant method for the outcome, though the BPD component requires some clinical judgment and the protocol does not establish external validation for this exact trial implementation. The evidence therefore supports probably not inappropriate.",
            "justification": "The composite includes objectively recorded death and a protocol-defined BPD component at 36 weeks PMA. BPD criteria incorporate oxygen/respiratory-support thresholds after at least 28 days of support; where oxygen need is subjective, an oxygen-reduction test confirms dependency using an oxygen-saturation threshold. This is a structured, clinically relevant method for the outcome, though the BPD component requires some clinical judgment and the protocol does not establish external validation for this exact trial implementation. The evidence therefore supports probably not inappropriate.",
            "unknowns": [
              "The oxygen-reduction test flowchart was not visually inspectable in the tool response; the applicable textual criteria were inspected."
