            "question_id": "sq:measurement:differential",
            "question": "Could measurement or ascertainment of the outcome have differed between intervention groups?",
            "driver": false,
            "answer": "probably_no",
            "facts": [],
            "warrant": "The same 36-week assessment point, BPD criteria, and oxygen-reduction approach apply to both randomized groups; trial personnel and outcome assessors were blinded. For eligible infants, oxygen-reduction testing was not performed in similar proportions (13/86 vs 13/94). No group-specific threshold or assessment method is reported. This supports probably no differential measurement; the exact assessment opportunity for every participant is not fully detailed.",
            "justification": "The same 36-week assessment point, BPD criteria, and oxygen-reduction approach apply to both randomized groups; trial personnel and outcome assessors were blinded. For eligible infants, oxygen-reduction testing was not performed in similar proportions (13/86 vs 13/94). No group-specific threshold or assessment method is reported. This supports probably no differential measurement; the exact assessment opportunity for every participant is not fully detailed.",
